{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>In a flood.</b> It has no [cognate with the root] ra, and the meaning is like \"a little.\"" "<b>And with everlasting kindness.</b> The opposite of \"a moment.\" The meaning is that the kingdom of Israel shall endure forever, as is explicit in the book of Daniel (Daniel 7:27). The days of exile, even if they lengthen, are like a moment compared to the days of the kingdom, which shall never cease."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 54, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:29.515206971Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}